{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "lem:full-data-local-polynomial-control",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "On every successful normalized-shape fit,\n\\[\n\\sum_{t=1}^{T}\\sum_{i=1}^{n_s}|a_{stik}|\n\\le\\{L_{sk}e_0^\\top G_{sk}^{-1}e_0\\}^{1/2}\n\\le c_G^{-1/2}.\n\\]\nBecause weights and covariates do not depend on the replicated-unit index,\n\\[\n\\sum_t|a_{stik}|\\le \\frac{c_G^{-1/2}}{n_s},\n\\qquad\n\\sum_t|\\bar a_{sti}|\\le \\frac{c_G^{-1/2}}{n_s},\n\\]\nand consequently\n\\[\n\\sum_{s=1}^{S}\\sum_{i=1}^{n_s}\n\\left[\\pi_s\\sum_t|\\bar a_{sti}|\\right]^2\n\\le c_G^{-1}R_{\\mathrm{tr}}.\n\\]\nThe exact Taylor bias is bounded by \\(A_L\\).  These deterministic conclusions require no upper local-mass event.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "T",
      "n_s",
      "s",
      "k",
      "a_stik",
      "L_sk",
      "e_0",
      "G_sk",
      "c_G",
      "bar_a_sti",
      "pi_s",
      "R_tr",
      "A_L"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:feasible-estimator",
      "def:honest-interval",
      "ass:holder-smoothness"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Suppress \\((s,k)\\), write \\(\\mathsf L=L_{sk}\\), and write \\(v_{ti}=w_{stk}^{1/2}b_r(u_{stk})\\).  Since\n\\[\nG=\\sum_{t,i}v_{ti}v_{ti}^\\top,\n\\qquad\na_{ti}=w_{stk}^{1/2}e_0^\\top G^{-1}v_{ti},\n\\]\nCauchy--Schwarz gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sum_{t,i}|a_{ti}|\n&\\le\n\\left\\{\\sum_{t,i}(e_0^\\top G^{-1}v_{ti})^2\\right\\}^{1/2}\n\\left\\{\\sum_{t,i}w_{stk}\\right\\}^{1/2}\\\\\n&=\\{e_0^\\top G^{-1}GG^{-1}e_0\\}^{1/2}\\mathsf L^{1/2}\n=\\{\\mathsf Le_0^\\top G^{-1}e_0\\}^{1/2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe selector's shape inequality is \\(G/\\mathsf L\\succeq c_GI\\), so \\(G^{-1}\\preceq(c_G\\mathsf L)^{-1}I\\).  Because \\(e_0=b_r(0)\\) is the constant-monomial coordinate and has Euclidean norm one under the declared monomial basis,\n\\[\n\\mathsf Le_0^\\top G^{-1}e_0\\le c_G^{-1}.\n\\]\nFor fixed \\((s,t,k)\\), neither \\(w_{stk}\\) nor \\(u_{stk}\\) depends on \\(i\\), while \\(G=n_s\\sum_tw_{stk}b_r(u_{stk})b_r(u_{stk})^\\top\\).  Thus \\(a_{stik}\\) is the same for every \\(i\\), and\n\\[\nn_s\\sum_t|a_{stik}|=\\sum_{t,i}|a_{stik}|\\le c_G^{-1/2}.\n\\]\nThe triangle inequality after averaging the fixed number of folds gives the same bound for \\(\\bar a_{sti}\\).  Therefore\n\\[\n\\sum_{s,i}\\left[\\pi_s\\sum_t|\\bar a_{sti}|\\right]^2\n\\le\\sum_sn_s\\left(\\frac{\\pi_sc_G^{-1/2}}{n_s}\\right)^2\n=c_G^{-1}\\sum_s\\frac{\\pi_s^2}{n_s}\n=c_G^{-1}R_{\\mathrm{tr}}.\n\\]\nFinally, the normal equations reproduce every polynomial of degree at most \\(r\\).  Subtracting the degree-\\(r\\) Taylor polynomial of \\(m_s\\) at \\(\\widetilde z_{sk}\\), applying the Holder remainder\n\\[\n|m_s(x)-T_{r,\\widetilde z_{sk}}m_s(x)|\n\\le C_{r,d}L\\|x-\\widetilde z_{sk}\\|_2^\\lambda,\n\\]\nand summing absolute weighted remainders gives exactly the displayed definition of \\(A_L\\).  No bound on \\(L_{sk}\\) from above was used.",
